  "formalConditions": "Current official prospective pages provide one indicative 2027-intake pathway:2027–2028 year 1 twelve 5 EC compulsory courses (60 EC);2028–2029 year 2 six 5 EC compulsory courses plus two Faculty of Arts minors of 15 EC, one each semester (60 EC);2029–2030 home-study year 3 four 5 EC compulsory courses,10 EC thesis and 30 EC free electives (60 EC). These pages explicitly say provisional, subject to change and no rights derived; they are not future formal regulations. Third-year students remaining in the Netherlands normally take 15 EC of free electives per semester. The abroad route has a different 30 EC specialist/compulsory allocation and is not combined with this pathway. Year 1 RADAr academic language proficiency and mentoring, and year 2 mentorship, are listed at 0 EC and remain additional obligations. The overview gives a 45 of 60 EC first-year positive BSA threshold, subject to personal circumstances. An educational minor is optional, taught in Dutch, and confers a bounded lower-secondary qualification; it is not an automatic outcome of the ordinary BA. No undisclosed thesis-entry threshold is invented.",
